# UCIEngine::on_update_full and SearchManager::output_pv, read 2026-11-24.
# D12, D13 and fisher-8hc answers 5 and 6 (2026-11-24) set the requested
# counts, numbering and bestmove. Ties leave the moves open (D5, D48 and
# the 2026-11-27 comment on fisher-8hc).
# Enumeration: python-chess 1.11.2 (https://pypi.org/project/chess/1.11.2/).
# Position from mate-in-one.uci. Apply fisher-2aj rules 2 to 5 to every
# root move and every legal reply: at depth 1 all 23 moves leave White
# up a queen (cp 900), even g6g7, since the horizon scores material.
# At depth 2 only g6g7 checkmates before the horizon (one ply, mate 1).
# Seven root moves stalemate (cp 0). After g6g8 or g6h7, Black's king
# captures the queen (cp 0). The other 13 leave the queen after every
# reply (cp 900). The best three scores are mate 1, cp 900 and cp 900.

> setoption name MultiPV value 3
> position fen 7k/8/5KQ1/8/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1
> go depth 2
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 1 multipv 2 score cp 900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 1 multipv 3 score cp 900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score mate 1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv g6g7
< info depth 2 multipv 2 score cp 900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 3 score cp 900 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove g6g7
> quit
! exit
